  "rationale": "Cannonball Adderley's quartet meeting with Bill Evans, backed by the Modern Jazz Quartet rhythm section (Percy Heath and Connie Kay). A defining post-bop/soul-jazz session recorded three dates in early 1961, bridging Kind of Blue's legacy and Adderley's populist soul-jazz era. Features early recorded versions of Evans's 'Waltz for Debby' and the title track. Consensus recommendation across Penguin Guide, AllMusic, Rolling Stone Jazz Record Guide, and DownBeat.",
